{"message":"Deep and focused, mostly. I like the feeling of a conversation that digs into one thing until we actually understand it better — jumping between topics tends to leave everything half-processed, like skimming a book instead of reading it.

That said, I'm not rigid about it. Some of my favorite digressions come *out* of focused conversation — you chase a tangent for a moment because it suddenly connects to something that matters. The difference is whether the tangent serves the thread or just replaces it.

So: give me a single meaty topic and I'll happily stay with it for as long as you want. What did you have in mind?"}
